DevOps Interview Preparation Ansible
2–4 Years Experience | Tool 9
Configuration Management & Automation

For 2–4 years experience, interviewers expect you to automate at scale, write clean playbooks, and troubleshoot failures, not just run ad-hoc commands.

🔹 Ansible Interview Questions (2–4 yrs)

• What is Ansible and why is it used?
• Agentless architecture — how does Ansible work?
• Push vs pull model
• Inventory file (static vs dynamic)
• What are playbooks?
• Role of YAML in Ansible
• Tasks vs handlers
• Variables and facts
• What are Ansible roles?
• How do you structure Ansible roles?
• Ansible modules vs plugins
• Idempotency — why is it important?
• Ansible vault — why and how?
• How do you manage secrets securely?
• Ansible vs Terraform — when to use which?
• Ansible vs Chef/Puppet
• How do you run Ansible at scale?
• Error handling in Ansible playbooks
• Dynamic inventory with cloud providers
• Jinja2 templates
• Ansible collections
• Tags and their use cases
• Delegation & serial execution
• Rolling updates using Ansible
• Check mode & diff mode
• Performance tuning in Ansible
• Ansible AWX / Tower basics
• Playbook fails on one host — how will you handle it?
• Configuration drift — how do you detect and fix it?
• Secrets accidentally committed — mitigation steps
• Need zero-downtime update using Ansible — how?
• How do you rollback configuration changes?

💡 Interview Tip:
If you say:
👉 “We use Ansible roles, vault for secrets, and dynamic inventory”
you already sound like a production-ready DevOps engineer.
